{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "00YJ", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-sites-enough-points}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:66d9b9a135f9f265b2be361891c34e3e5133268aa6356f11ef9d9b1dd2fe3508", "source_text": "Sites with enough points", "source_text_hash": "sha256:50d584d683df5eb46b7c617bd1049e5bb97f2ab77a1e262a97852204b5318487", "unit_id": "tag:00YJ:title"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "00YJ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\{p_i\\}_{i\\in I}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\phi : \\mathcal{F} \\to \\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{F}_{p_i}\n\\to \\mathcal{G}_{p_i}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-enough-points}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ebe2480a8cbaa92bb8525d199f33cadced91f8b100dd076f181295b83d1c1d9e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ad365f51203c01b21d7b1cb02e7cea6e7a9b9c54ad6e90439b41c1c21983b919", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a site.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> A family of points <MATH_0002> is called <TEXTITOPEN_0001>conservative<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>\nif every map of sheaves <MATH_0003>\nwhich is an isomorphism on all the fibres <MATH_0004> is an isomorphism.\n<STRUCT_0003>  We say that <MATH_0005> <TEXTITOPEN_0002>has enough points<TEXTITCLOSE_0002>\nif there exists a conservative family of points.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b959b1604cb5216e1e5e4f4d4a6450078245fa12887dd5c65c44fc2fb5e6c5df", "unit_id": "tag:00YK:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "00YJ", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:362bff2da7e3367e1509650f71e74e02db25a0a7786b65a8b16bbd422cf8c095", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIt turns out that you can then check ``exactness'' at the stalks.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6d5c917616e5b3962da4c73a14c3a7ab981c5123ec8a431241c2ce6732fa9a92", "unit_id": "tag:00YJ:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "00YJ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\{p_i\\}_{i\\in I}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\varphi : \\mathcal{F} \\to \\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\forall i, \\varphi_{p_i}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\varphi$", "MATH_0006": "$\\varphi : \\mathcal{F} \\to \\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\forall i, \\varphi_{p_i}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\varphi$", "MATH_0009": "$\\varphi_1, \\varphi_2 : \\mathcal{F} \\to \\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0010": "$\\forall i, \\varphi_{1, p_i} = \\varphi_{2, p_i}$", "MATH_0011": "$\\varphi_1 = \\varphi_2$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{G} : \\mathcal{J}\n\\to \\Sh(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0013": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0014": "$q_j : \\mathcal{F} \\to \\mathcal{G}_j$", "MATH_0015": "$(\\mathcal{F}, q_j)$", "MATH_0016": "$i$", "MATH_0017": "$(\\mathcal{F}_{p_i}, (q_j)_{p_i})$", "MATH_0018": "$\\mathcal{F} : \\mathcal{J}\n\\to \\Sh(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0019": "$\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0020": "$e_j : \\mathcal{F}_j \\to \\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0021": "$(\\mathcal{G}, e_j)$", "MATH_0022": "$i$", "MATH_0023": "$(\\mathcal{G}_{p_i}, (e_j)_{p_i})$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "STRUCT_0006": "\\item", "STRUCT_0007": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-exactness-stalks}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:4627abca5c3816b4658903771f9047021ba4cda468f2fc2b7eaf596f46e613b0", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:47ba15e7e26fed89f663912f296999264bdad4cd179fcd8cf1f80a7d4a8b500f", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a site and let <MATH_0002> be a conservative\nfamily of points. Then\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> Given any map of sheaves <MATH_0003>\nwe have <MATH_0004> injective implies <MATH_0005> injective.\n<STRUCT_0003> Given any map of sheaves <MATH_0006>\nwe have <MATH_0007> surjective implies <MATH_0008> surjective.\n<STRUCT_0004> Given any pair of maps of sheaves\n<MATH_0009>\nwe have <MATH_0010>\nimplies <MATH_0011>.\n<STRUCT_0005> Given a finite diagram <MATH_0012>, a sheaf <MATH_0013> and morphisms\n<MATH_0014> then <MATH_0015>\nis a limit of the diagram if and only if for each <MATH_0016> the stalk\n<MATH_0017> is one.\n<STRUCT_0006> Given a finite diagram <MATH_0018>, a sheaf <MATH_0019> and morphisms\n<MATH_0020> then <MATH_0021>\nis a colimit of the diagram if and only if for each <MATH_0022> the stalk\n<MATH_0023> is one.\n<STRUCT_0007>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e4e025fd60a35cef47aeb79fc32194bc7354b0bcf97e2a0ce600ba87b891bd04", "unit_id": "tag:00YL:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "00YJ", "placeholders": {"FOOTNOTECLOSE_0001": "}", "FOOTNOTEOPEN_0001": "\\footnote{", "MATH_0001": "$\\varphi : \\mathcal{F} \\to \\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F} \\to \\mathcal{F} \\times_\\mathcal{G} \\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\varphi : \\mathcal{F} \\to \\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{G} \\amalg_\\mathcal{F} \\mathcal{G} \\to \\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0005": "$a, b : \\mathcal{F} \\to \\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\text{Equalizer}(a, b : \\mathcal{F} \\to \\mathcal{G}) \\to \\mathcal{F}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{categories-lemma-finite-limits-exist}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:575df184bc3ed57f92d4e4d874355ff510749027e2957cbbc16cf87ca76da837", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:78ee9596e9a7411ef3d543836f6eee0b957067c98b6b93abffa97e0b6f6458c7", "source_text": "We will use over and over again that all the stalk functors commute\nwith any finite limits and colimits and hence with products, fibred\nproducts, etc. We will also use that injective maps are the monomorphisms\nand the surjective maps are the epimorphisms.\nA map of sheaves <MATH_0001>\nis injective if and only if\n<MATH_0002>\nis an isomorphism. Hence (1).\nSimilarly, <MATH_0003>\nis surjective if and only if\n<MATH_0004>\nis an isomorphism. Hence (2).\nThe maps <MATH_0005>\nare equal if and only if\n<MATH_0006>\nis an isomorphism<FOOTNOTEOPEN_0001>The equalizer can be expressed\nin terms of products and fibre products, see proof of\nCategories, Lemma <REF_0001>.<FOOTNOTECLOSE_0001>. Hence (3).\nThe assertions (4) and (5) follow immediately from the definitions\nand the remarks at the start of this proof.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a603ef1c311f478b87fcc73280bda57ba9d3fe4716065124e3d894432bede126", "unit_id": "tag:00YL:proof"}
