he lemma.\n\n<STRUCT_0001><STRUCT_0002>\nTo prove the converse, assume the condition on the existence of\npoints of the lemma. Let <MATH_0015>\nbe a map of sheaves which is an isomorphism at all the stalks.\nWe have to show that <MATH_0016> is both\ninjective and surjective, see Lemma <REF_0004>.\nInjectivity is an immediate consequence of the assumption.\nTo show surjectivity we have to show that\n<MATH_0017>\nis an isomorphism\n(Categories, Lemma <REF_0005>).\nSince this map is clearly surjective, it suffices to check injectivity\nwhich follows as <MATH_0018>\nis injective on all stalks by assumption.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:58bdc394468565fa0e4c403b1a4e033821e20f12a9d552e02aa85630cd635fa4", "unit_id": "tag:00YM:proof"}
